---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const aboutJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: 'About Annotated Papers by Chris Hayduk',
  url: new URL('/about', Astro.site).toString(),
  description: 'Explanations of biological AI papers, with PyTorch implementations and interactive figures.',
  author: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Chris Hayduk',
    url: 'https://chrishayduk.com',
  },
  inLanguage: 'en',
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About — Annotated Papers by Chris Hayduk"
  description="About Annotated Papers by Chris Hayduk: explanations of biological AI papers, with PyTorch code and interactive figures."
  jsonLd={aboutJsonLd}
>
  <article class="about-page">
    <header class="about-header">
      <div class="about-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">About the project</p>
        <h1>Why I annotate<br /><span>research papers.</span></h1>
        <p class="about-lede">
          These notes explain the equations and implementation details in biological AI papers,
          with code and figures alongside the text.
        </p>
        <a class="author-link" href="https://chrishayduk.com" rel="me">
          <span class="author-monogram" aria-hidden="true">CH</span>
          <span>A project by <strong>Chris Hayduk</strong></span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <aside class="reading-note" aria-label="The approach">
        <p class="eyebrow">In each annotation</p>
        <ol>
          <li><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><strong>Explanatory notes</strong><p>Architecture, equations, and notation.</p></div></li>
          <li><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><strong>PyTorch code</strong><p>Excerpts from the companion implementation.</p></div></li>
          <li><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><strong>Interactive figures</strong><p>Diagrams and controls for specific mechanisms.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="reading-note-footer">With references to the paper and source code.</p>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <div class="about-body">
      <nav class="about-contents" aria-label="On this page">
        <p class="eyebrow">On this page</p>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#purpose"><span>01</span> Purpose</a></li>
          <li><a href="#method"><span>02</span> Format</a></li>
          <li><a href="#provenance"><span>03</span> Source code</a></li>
          <li><a href="#current"><span>04</span> AlphaFold2</a></li>
          <li><a href="#practice"><span>05</span> BioTorch</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <div class="about-sections">
        <section id="purpose">
          <p class="eyebrow">01 / Purpose</p>
          <h2>The details between the equations</h2>
          <p>
            Papers describe new results for readers who already know the field. They often leave
            intermediate calculations implicit, and put implementation details in a supplement or
            a separate codebase. That can make a model difficult to reconstruct from the paper alone.
          </p>
          <p>
            I use this site to explain those details: what an equation computes, which dimensions
            a tensor has, and how an operation is implemented. The original paper remains the
            reference for the research; the annotation provides additional explanation and code.
          </p>
          <p>
            The format is inspired by
            <a href="https://nlp.seas.harvard.edu/annotated-transformer/">The Annotated Transformer</a>,
            which presents an implementation alongside an explanation of the paper.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="method">
          <p class="eyebrow">02 / Format</p>
          <h2>How the annotations are organized</h2>
          <p>
            Each annotation is divided into sections for the model's components. The table of contents
            links to individual sections, and the notes refer to the relevant equations and code.
          </p>
          <ol class="method-list">
            <li>
              <div class="method-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M6 3h9l3 3v15H6V3Z" /><path d="M14 3v5h4M9 12h6M9 16h6" /></svg>
              </div>
              <div><h3>Paper and notation</h3><p>
                The text explains the architecture and equations using notation close to the
                original. References let you compare the explanation with the paper and supplement.
              </p></div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <div class="method-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="m8 6-5 6 5 6m8-12 5 6-5 6M14 4l-4 16" /></svg>
              </div>
              <div><h3>Implementation</h3><p>
                Code excerpts come from a runnable implementation. They include tensor shapes
                and variables corresponding to the paper's notation. The repository contains the
                complete source.
              </p></div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <div class="method-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M5 3v18M12 3v18M19 3v18" /><path d="M2 8h6v4H2zM9 14h6v4H9zM16 6h6v4h-6z" fill="currentColor" /></svg>
              </div>
              <div><h3>Interactive figures</h3><p>
                Some sections include figures with adjustable views or parameters, so you can
                inspect the operation described in the text.
              </p></div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section id="provenance">
          <p class="eyebrow">03 / Source code</p>
          <h2>Code and reproducibility</h2>
          <p>
            The companion implementations prioritize readable code and include unit and
            integration tests. Each annotation refers to a specific repository commit, so the
            excerpts can be checked against the exact version of the source.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can clone the repository to run the implementation locally. The repository's
            documentation describes its setup and scope.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="current" class="current-paper">
          <p class="eyebrow">04 / Current annotation</p>
          <h2>The Annotated AlphaFold2</h2>
          <p>
            The first annotation covers AlphaFold2, including the Evoformer, Invariant Point
            Attention, the Structure Module, and frame-aligned point error (FAPE). Code excerpts
            come from the companion PyTorch implementation,
            <a href="https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/minAlphaFold2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">minAlphaFold2</a>.
          </p>
          <div class="current-links">
            <a class="button-primary" href="/alphafold2">Read the annotation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
            <a class="button-secondary" href="https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/minAlphaFold2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              View the repository <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="practice" class="practice-note">
          <p class="eyebrow">05 / Related project</p>
          <h2>PyTorch exercises on BioTorch</h2>
          <p>
            I also maintain BioTorch, a site with coding exercises drawn from biological AI
            models. Each problem asks you to implement a specific operation in PyTorch, with
            tensor shapes, examples, and tests.
          </p>
          <a class="practice-link" href="https://biotorch.chrishayduk.com">
            Browse BioTorch exercises <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </section>

        <footer class="author-note">
          <p>Annotated Papers by <a href="https://chrishayduk.com" rel="me">Chris Hayduk</a>.</p>
          <a href="/">Back to the papers <span aria-hidden="true">↑</span></a>
        </footer>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    width: min(100% - 4rem, 76rem);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .about-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(17rem, 0.8fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }

  .about-intro > .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .about-header h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 4.8vw, 4.2rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    line-height: 1.08;
  }
  .about-header h1 span { color: var(--accent); }
  .about-lede {
    max-width: 37rem;
    margin: 1.65rem 0 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.5vw, 1.17rem);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .author-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .author-link strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 600; }
  .author-link:hover strong { color: var(--accent); }
  .author-monogram {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 2.2rem;
    height: 2.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .reading-note {
    padding: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 0.8rem;
    background: var(--surface-strong);
  }
  .reading-note > .eyebrow { font-size: 0.59rem; }
  .reading-note ol { list-style: none; margin: 1.75rem 0; padding: 0; }
  .reading-note li { display: flex; align-items: start; gap: 1rem; }
  .reading-note li + li { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .reading-note li > span {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    flex: 0 0 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 0.35rem;
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
  }
  .reading-note strong { font-size: 0.86rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .reading-note li p { margin: 0.35rem 0 0; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: 0.73rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .reading-note-footer { margin: 0; padding-top: 1.15rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: 0.68rem; line-height: 1.7; }

  .about-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 15rem minmax(0, 43rem);
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 7rem);
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
  }
  .about-contents { display: block; align-self: start; position: sticky; top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem); }
  .about-contents > p { margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  .about-contents ol { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .about-contents li + li { margin-top: 0.35rem; }
  .about-contents a { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.85rem; min-height: 2.35rem; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: 0.8rem; text-decoration: none; }
  .about-contents a span { color: var(--accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.63rem; }
  .about-contents a:hover { color: var(--accent); }

  .about-sections { min-width: 0; }
  .about-sections > section { scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem); padding-bottom: 3.5rem; }
  .about-sections > section + section { padding-top: 3.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .about-sections .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .about-sections h2 { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 2.5vw, 2.15rem); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1.2; }
  .about-sections section > p:not(.eyebrow), .method-list p { margin: 0; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.85; }
  .about-sections section > p + p { margin-top: 1.15rem; }
  .about-sections section > p a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration-color: var(--rule-strong); text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }
  .about-sections section > p a:hover { text-decoration-color: var(--accent); }

  .method-list { margin: 1.75rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .method-list li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2.5rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1.2rem; padding-block: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .method-list li:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; }
  .method-icon { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 2.5rem; height: 2.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 0.45rem; background: var(--surface); color: var(--accent); }
  .method-icon svg { width: 1.2rem; height: 1.2rem; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .method-list h3 { margin: 0 0 0.45rem; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .method-list p { font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .current-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  .current-links a { font-size: 0.8rem; }

  .about-sections > .practice-note { padding: 2.2rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 0.7rem; background: var(--accent-soft); }
  .practice-note h2 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.3vw, 1.85rem); }
  .practice-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 650; text-decoration: none; }
  .practice-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.3em; }
  .author-note { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding-top: 2rem; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .author-note p { margin: 0; }
  .author-note a { color: var(--accent); text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }
  .author-note > a { text-decoration: none; }
  .author-note > a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .author-note > a span { margin-left: 0.65rem; }

  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .about-header { gap: 2.5rem; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(16rem, 0.8fr); }
    .reading-note { padding: 1.5rem; }
    .about-body { grid-template-columns: 12rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 3rem; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .about-page { width: min(100% - 2.5rem, 76rem); }
    .about-header { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; }
    .about-header h1 { font-size: clamp(2.55rem, 7vw, 3.5rem); }
    .reading-note { max-width: 36rem; }
    .about-body { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; }
    .about-contents { position: static; padding-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
    .about-contents ol { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.2rem 1.5rem; }
    .about-contents li + li { margin-top: 0; }
    .about-contents a { min-height: 2.5rem; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .about-page { width: min(100% - 2rem, 76rem); }
    .about-header { padding-block: 3rem; }
    .about-sections > section { padding-bottom: 2.75rem; }
    .about-sections > section + section { padding-top: 2.75rem; }
    .about-sections > .practice-note { padding: 1.5rem; }
    .current-links { align-items: stretch; flex-direction: column; }
    .current-links a { justify-content: center; }
    .method-list li { grid-template-columns: 2rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0.9rem; }
    .method-icon { width: 2rem; height: 2rem; }
  }
</style>
